### Description

With `JSON_DIAGNOSTIC_POSITIONS` alone, an exception about the **root** value of a parsed document names its byte range, e.g. `(bytes 0-4)`. As soon as `JSON_DIAGNOSTICS` is enabled as well, the root value's exception loses the byte range, while nested values keep both the path and the range:

| build | `json::parse("true").get<std::string>()` | `json::parse("[1, true]")[1].get<std::string>()` |
|---|---|---|
| `JSON_DIAGNOSTIC_POSITIONS=1` | `[json.exception.type_error.302] (bytes 0-4) type must be string, but is boolean` | `… (bytes 4-8) type must be string, but is boolean` |
| both macros | `[json.exception.type_error.302] type must be string, but is boolean` | `… (/1) (bytes 4-8) type must be string, but is boolean` |

Nothing in the [`JSON_DIAGNOSTIC_POSITIONS` documentation](https://json.nlohmann.me/api/macros/json_diagnostic_positions/) excludes the root value; its combined example only shows a nested value, and no test combines both macros on a root exception (`tests/src/unit-diagnostic-positions.cpp` lines 195-210 cover nested values only).

**Root cause.** `exception::diagnostics()` returns early when the path has no tokens ([exceptions.hpp#L201-L204](https://github.com/nlohmann/json/blob/ddc34f546a652cd098dd78225d80f1909b921871/include/nlohmann/detail/exceptions.hpp#L201-L204)), before `get_byte_positions()` is appended at [#L212](https://github.com/nlohmann/json/blob/ddc34f546a652cd098dd78225d80f1909b921871/include/nlohmann/detail/exceptions.hpp#L212):

```cpp
        if (tokens.empty())
        {
            return "";
        }
        …
        return concat('(', str, ") ", get_byte_positions(leaf_element));
```

The early return is from 2021 (74cc0ab470, before positions existed); #4585 appended the byte positions after it without revisiting it, although the discussion in #4561 intended that with both options set the message carries both. The json_view implementation copies the same early return ([view/errors.hpp#L260-L264](https://github.com/nlohmann/json/blob/ddc34f546a652cd098dd78225d80f1909b921871/include/nlohmann/detail/view/errors.hpp#L260-L264)), so `json_document::parse("true").root().get<std::string>()` behaves the same way in all three builds.

**Since when.** 3.12.0 (the release that added `JSON_DIAGNOSTIC_POSITIONS`); reproduced with the 3.12.0 single header.

**Possible fix.** In both functions, build the path prefix only when there are tokens and always append the byte range:

```cpp
        std::string prefix;
        if (!tokens.empty())
        {
            auto str = std::accumulate(…);
            prefix = concat('(', str, ") ");
        }
        return concat(prefix, get_byte_positions(leaf_element));
```

plus a test in `unit-diagnostic-positions.cpp` with both macros on a root value (and one in `unit-json_view_positions.cpp`).

### Reproduction steps

1. Save the program below as `rootpos.cpp`.
2. `clang++ -std=c++17 -DJSON_DIAGNOSTIC_POSITIONS=1 -I include rootpos.cpp -o p1 && ./p1`
3. `clang++ -std=c++17 -DJSON_DIAGNOSTIC_POSITIONS=1 -DJSON_DIAGNOSTICS=1 -I include rootpos.cpp -o p2 && ./p2`

### Expected vs. actual results

Expected (step 3): `true root: [json.exception.type_error.302] (bytes 0-4) type must be string, but is boolean`, like step 2.

Actual (step 3): `true root: [json.exception.type_error.302] type must be string, but is boolean`, while the nested value prints `(/1) (bytes 4-8)`.

### Minimal code example

```cpp
#include <nlohmann/json.hpp>
#include <cstdio>
using json = nlohmann::json;
int main()
{
    for (const char* t : {"true", "[1, true]"})
    {
        json j = json::parse(t);
        try { (void)j.get<std::string>(); } catch (const json::exception& e) { std::printf("%s root: %s\n", t, e.what()); }
        if (j.is_array())
        {
            try { (void)j[1].get<std::string>(); } catch (const json::exception& e) { std::printf("%s /1:   %s\n", t, e.what()); }
        }
    }
}
```

### Error messages

```
$ ./p1
true root: [json.exception.type_error.302] (bytes 0-4) type must be string, but is boolean
[1, true] root: [json.exception.type_error.302] (bytes 0-9) type must be string, but is array
[1, true] /1:   [json.exception.type_error.302] (bytes 4-8) type must be string, but is boolean
$ ./p2
true root: [json.exception.type_error.302] type must be string, but is boolean
[1, true] root: [json.exception.type_error.302] type must be string, but is array
[1, true] /1:   [json.exception.type_error.302] (/1) (bytes 4-8) type must be string, but is boolean
```

### Compiler and operating system

Apple clang 21.0.0 (clang-2100.3.34.2), macOS 27.

### Library version

develop at ddc34f546a (2026-11-01) and 3.12.0.

### Validation

- [x] The bug also occurs if the latest version from the [`develop`](https://github.com/nlohmann/json/tree/develop) branch is used.
- [x] I can successfully [compile and run the unit tests](https://github.com/nlohmann/json#execute-unit-tests).

---
*Found by a json_view-vs-DOM differential test during a bug hunt; written by Claude Code on behalf of @nlohmann.*
